# =============================================================================
# NEWS2 staleness windows -- DEMONSTRATION PROFILE (HD-E7)
#
# NOT CLINICALLY VALIDATED. For the synthetic demo (run_demo.*, docker
# compose) only. A deployment that sees real patients must replace every value
# with windows approved and signed by its clinical safety officer (HD-E4) and
# recorded in RMF-001; the gateway deliberately has NO built-in default and
# refuses to start until all seven are set.
#
# How these demo values were chosen (rationale, not a clinical claim):
# - A reading older than its window is excluded from scoring, so a short
#   window is the conservative direction: the score is withheld rather than
#   computed from out-of-date data.
# - Continuously monitored parameters (heart rate, SpO2, respiratory rate) are
#   streamed by bedside monitors every few seconds; 5 minutes of silence
#   already indicates a disconnected or failed sensor.
# - Non-invasive blood pressure is typically cycled every 15-30 minutes in
#   monitored settings; 30 minutes.
# - Supplemental O2 status changes are charted; 1 hour.
# - Temperature and ACVPU are nursing observations; RCP NEWS2 (2017) sets a
#   minimum observation frequency of 4-6 hourly for an aggregate score of 1-4.
#   4 hours is the tighter end of that range.
# =============================================================================
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_HEART_RATE_SECONDS=300
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_SPO2_SECONDS=300
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_RESPIRATORY_RATE_SECONDS=300
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_SYSTOLIC_BP_SECONDS=1800
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_SUPPLEMENTAL_O2_SECONDS=3600
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_TEMPERATURE_CELSIUS_SECONDS=14400
NEWS2_STALENESS_WINDOW_CONSCIOUSNESS_SECONDS=14400
